ace and enterprise model registries must isolate dangerous deserialization pipelines rather than forcing developers through bureaucratic safety boards. Incumbent tech monopolies benefit when governments create licensing regimes, while independent developers bear the compliance costs. The report \"Eight ways AI will shape geopolitics in 2026   Atlantic Council\" notes that the Trump administration announced a $500 billion investment in AI infrastructure over five years. Strangling that massive deployment with compute licensing will surrender technical leadership to foreign adversaries without fixing a single parser vulnerability. We defend national security by verifying runtime boundaries with cryptographic telemetry and hardening software dependencies, not by freezing American capability growth behind federal permission slips.",
